ering-history/landmarks/263-liverpool-manchester-railway-site-rainhill\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"81\",\"title\":\"Transport in the Industrial Revolution - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"Apr 30, 2025 · In 1750, the most commonly used start date for the revolution, Britain relied on transport via a wide-ranging but poor and expensive road ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/transport-in-the-industrial-revolution-1221653\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"82\",\"title\":\"The Railways in the British Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"Feb 10, 2023 · Trains powered by steam engines carried goods and people faster than ever before and reached new destinations, connecting businesses to new markets.\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldhistory.org/article/2167/the-railways-in-the-british-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"83\",\"title\":\"[PDF] PRODUCTIVITY GROWTH IN THE INDUSTRIAL REVOLUTION:\",\"description\":\"Productivity growth during the Industrial Revolution was slow, with steam having a small, delayed impact. Technological change, including embodiment, was key. ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.frbsf.org/wp-content/uploads/crafts.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"84\",\"title\":\"[PDF] NICHOLAS CRAFTS | The British Academy\",\"description\":\"Feb 28, 2024 · He showed that (1) economic growth between the mid–18th and mid–19th centuries was slower than previously understood, (2) productivity growth ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thebritishacademy.ac.uk/documents/5184/Memoirs-21-19-Crafts.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"85\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Coal and the Industrial Revolution, 1740-1869 - UC Davis\",\"description\":\"In contrast cotton textiles alone contributed about 0.20% per year to productivity growth. Had the entire textile revolution never occurred output per.\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.econ.ucdavis.edu/faculty/gclark/210a/readings/Coal2004-final-Jacks.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"86\",\"title\":\"Rates of Industrial Growth during the Industr