proved the agricultural productivity of farms from the late 18th century by bringing more land into effective ...Missing:  labor | Show results with:labor\",\"url\":\"https://www.parliament.uk/about/living-heritage/transformingsociety/towncountry/landscape/overview/enclosingland/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"92\",\"title\":\"Capitalism in the Age of the Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"Expansion of Markets. Capitalism encouraged the relentless search for new markets to sell industrial goods. Entrepreneurs sought customers beyond local or ...\",\"url\":\"https://voicesofcapitalism.com/industrial-revolution-capitalism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"93\",\"title\":\"The Development of Banking in the Industrial Revolution - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"Apr 30, 2025 · In 1837 new laws gave joint-stock companies the ability to acquire limited liability, and in 1855 and 58 these laws were expanded, with banks ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/development-of-banking-the-industrial-revolution-1221645\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"94\",\"title\":\"[PDF] British Economic Growth 1760 - 1913 - University of Warwick\",\"description\":\"Most empirical investigation of the new growth theory has been undertaken looking at cross-sections of countries for the period since 1960 leading to well-known ...\",\"url\":\"https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/soc/economics/research/workingpapers/1989-1994/twerp415.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"95\",\"title\":\"Financial Institutions and the British Industrial Revolution - JoIE Blog\",\"description\":\"Jan 25, 2021 · The Bubble Act of 1720 put severe restriction on the formation of joint stock companies. It was not repealed until 1825. From 1714 to well ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://joie-blog.net/financial-institutions-and-the-british-industrial-revolution-did-financial-underdevelopment-hold-back-growth\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"96\",\"title\":\"How the Bank of England assisted in the formation of a fiscal-military ...\",\"description\":\"Sep 28, 2022 · We show how the Bank of England contributed to form an effective and efficient fiscal-naval state and promoted the development of a system of financial ...\",\"url\":\"https://ehs.org.uk/how-the-bank-of-england-assisted-in-the-formation-of-a-fiscal-military-state-in-britain/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"97\",\"title\":\"[PDF] HOW SOVEREIGN DEBT ACCELERATED THE FIRST INDUSTRIAL ...\",\"description\":\"It reviews the stylized facts of the Industrial Revolution and it also describes the main features of the British financial system. Section III presents our ...\",\"url\":\"https://economics.yale.edu/sites/default/files/joachim_voch_macrows_040516.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"98\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Banking and Innovation: Evidence from the Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"This paper provides new evidence that bank credit could alle- viate the credit constraints of industrialists and increase innovation in an emerging financial.\",\"url\":\"https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/soc/economics/staff/jwei/banking_and_innovation_jmp_jinlin_wei.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"99\",\"title\":\"Banks and patents during the British Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"Sep 12, 2023 · Country banks' short-term credit increased patenting, especially in manufacturing, by alleviating credit constraints and enabling fixed-capital ...\",\"url\":\"https://ehs.org.uk/banks-and-patents-during-the-british-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"100\",\"title\":\"Financial institutions and the British Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"Jan 22, 2021 · This scoping paper addresses the role of financial institutions in empowering the British Industrial Revolution.\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/journal-of-institutional-economics/article/financial-institutions-and-the-british-industrial-revolution-did-financial-underdevelopment-hold-back-growth/422EF61BFB7D0E952845F488FA13E350\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"101\",\"title\":\"The role of the banks (Chapter 11) - The First Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"One of the advantages with which Britain entered upon the first industrial revolution was a developed system of money and banking.\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/first-industrial-revolution/role-of-the-banks/080AE00A84C02FEC9A6AF2E60CB5DAB2\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"102\",\"title\":\"[PDF] How Did Growth Begin? The Industrial Revolution and its Antecedents\",\"description\":\"Growth During the Industrial Revolution,” Journal of Economic History, 42, 267–. 289. HATCHER, J. (1993): The History of the British Coal Industry, Volume I, ...Missing:  chronological | Show results with:chronological\",\"url\":\"https://eml.berkeley.edu/~jsteinsson/teaching/originsofgrowth.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"103\",\"title\":\"Population Growth and Movement in the Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"May 8, 2025 · Britain's population changed rapidly in the first industrial revolution, in terms of size and location along with cities and towns.Missing:  data | Show results with:data\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/population-growth-and-movement-industrial-revolution-1221640\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"104\",\"title\":\"Mortality, migration and epidemiological change in English cities ...\",\"description\":\"After 1800 the pace of urbanisation accelerated further, and London's growth also picked up, such that the capital accounted for 14 % of the English population ...\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7611108/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"105\",\"title\":\"Urbanisation and population growth in England, 1600 -1950. Urban...\",\"description\":\"At the time of the first census in 1801 30 % of the English population was already living in urban centres (with populations of 2,500 or more inhabitants, the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Urbanisation-and-population-growth-in-England-1600-1950-Urban-figures-refer-to-the_fig2_352490831\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"106\",\"title\":\"The first urban society\",\"description\":\"Oct 31, 2024 · Britain was the first society to become predominantly urban, with over half the population living in towns or cities by 1851.\",\"url\":\"https://www.campop.geog.cam.ac.uk/blog/2024/10/31/urban-society/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"107\",\"title\":\"Industrialisation and population growth, 1750-1860s - Bernard Deacon\",\"description\":\"From around 27% over the previous century, it reached 30% in the three decades from 1751 to 1781, 37% in the next three decades to 1811 and peaked at a 55% ...\",\"url\":\"https://bernarddeacon.com/demography/industrialisation-and-population-growth-1750-1860s/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"108\",\"title\":\"Urbanization and mortality in Britain, c. 1800–50 - PMC\",\"description\":\"This study finds good evidence for widespread increases in mortality in the second quarter of the nineteenth century.\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7186836/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"109\",\"title\":\"Urbanization and mortality in Britain, c. 1800–50 - Wiley Online Library\",\"description\":\"Feb 21, 2020 · This article reviews long-run historical relationships between urbanization and epidemiological trends in England, and then addresses the ...\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/ehr.12964\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"110\",\"title\":\"Structural change and economic growth in the British economy ...\",\"description\":\"Our results show that England experienced unusually early structural change and highlight the mid-seventeenth century as a turning point.\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6420141/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"111\",\"title\":\"[PDF] THE INDUSTRIAL REVOLUTION AS A DEMOGRAPHIC EVENT\",\"description\":\"... population growth in England in the years 1760-1860 was so different from previous population booms as in 1500-1630, and 1200-. 1300. Why did these earlier ...\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.econ.ucdavis.edu/faculty/gclark/210a/readings/irwash1.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"112\",\"title\":\"The First Factories | World History - Lumen Learning\",\"description\":\"The factory system was a new way of organizing labor made necessary by the development of machines, which were too large to house in a worker's cottage and much ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-worldhistory/chapter/25-2-3-the-first-factories/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"113\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://trdsf.com/blogs/news/industrial-revolution-the-emergence-of-the-factory-system-and-how-it-changed-the-world\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"114\",\"title\":\"Why did the Luddites protest? - The National Archives\",\"description\":\"Luddites were protesting against changes they thought would make their lives much worse, changes that were part of a new market system.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/education/resources/why-did-the-luddites-protest/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"115\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Pessimism Preserved: Real Wages in the British Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"Recently, however, Clark (2005) has argued that real wages grew much more rapidly than Feinstein and Allen thought.1 He has brought new prices sources and ...\",\"url\":\"http://piketty.pse.ens.fr/files/Allen2007a.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"116\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Pessimism Perpetuated: Real Wages and the Standard of Living in ...\",\"description\":\"The standard of living of the average working-class family improved by less than 15 percent between the 1780s and 1850s.\",\"url\":\"http://piketty.pse.ens.fr/files/Feinstein1998.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"117\",\"title\":\"Heights and Living Standards of English Workers During the Early ...\",\"description\":\"Falling heights of urban- and rural-born males after 1780 and a delayed growth spurt for 13- to 23-year-old boys revealed de