usually dated between 1870 and 1914, although a number of its char- acteristic events can be dated to the 1850s.\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.wcas.northwestern.edu/jmokyr/castronovo.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"188\",\"title\":\"Overview of the Second Industrial Revolution - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"Apr 26, 2021 · The Second Industrial Revolution took place from 1870 to 1914. Learn more about this period of unprecedented advancement in industry and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/second-industrial-revolution-overview-5180514\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"189\",\"title\":\"9.1 The Second Industrial Revolution - World History Volume 2, from ...\",\"description\":\"Dec 14, 2022 · Many developments of the Second Industrial Revolution built on or improved earlier technology. Mass production of steel, for example, ...\",\"url\":\"https://openstax.org/books/world-history-volume-2/pages/9-1-the-second-industrial-revolution\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"190\",\"title\":\"Henry Bessemer – Man of Steel - Features - The Chemical Engineer\",\"description\":\"Nov 1, 2010 · Patented in 1855, the Bessemer process decreased the cost of steel from £50–60/t ($80–95/t) to £6–7/t ($9–11/t), hand-in-hand with vast ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thechemicalengineer.com/features/cewctw-henry-bessemer-man-of-steel/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"191\",\"title\":\"The Bessemer Process: Revolutionizing Steelmaking - Endura Steel\",\"description\":\"Jul 14, 2023 · Here's a timeline of how this process came to be: 1856: Bessemer's Patent: Henry Bessemer obtained a patent for his new steelmaking method, ...\",\"url\":\"https://endura-steel.com/the-bessemer-process-revolutionizing-steelmaking-and-industrialization/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"192\",\"title\":\"Henry Bessemer, the wizard of steel who transformed cities - Sacyr\",\"description\":\"Nov 4, 2020 · With his new method of oxidation, he could convert 25 tons of iron into steel in 25 minutes. A year after he patented his method (1855), Henry ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://sacyr.com/en/-/henry-bessemer-el-mago-del-acero-que-transformo-las-ciudades\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"193\",\"title\":\"Dynamo machine - Siemens Global\",\"description\":\"In early December 1866, Werner von Siemens reported on his experiments with the new dynamo machine to his brother William. Looking at the commercial potential ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.siemens.com/global/en/company/about/history/stories/dynamo-machine.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"194\",\"title\":\"The History of the Light Bulb - Department of Energy\",\"description\":\"Nov 22, 2013 · By October 1879, Edison's team had produced a light bulb with a carbonized filament of uncoated cotton thread that could last for 14.5 hours.\",\"url\":\"https://www.energy.gov/articles/history-light-bulb\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"195\",\"title\":\"Conventional power plants - Siemens Global\",\"description\":\"1866: The dynamo machine. Werner von Siemens developed the dynamo machine – his most important invention – by reconfiguring a magneto with a double-T armature.\",\"url\":\"https://www.siemens.com/global/en/company/about/history/technology/power-generation-and-distribution/conventional-power-plants.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"196\",\"title\":\"How Nikolaus August Otto created the 4-stroke internal combustion ...\",\"description\":\"Nov 5, 2020 · In 1876, Otto developed a gaseous fuel, compressed charge 4-stroke cycle that would become known as the Otto-Cycle. This is the principle that ...\",\"url\":\"https://accelleron.com/charge-magazine/how-nikolaus-august-otto-created-the-4-stroke-internal-combustion-engine\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"197\",\"title\":\"Benz Patent Motor Car: The first automobile (1885–1886)\",\"description\":\"The Benz patent motor car Victoria is the first vehicle with the double-pivot steering for which Carl Benz filed a patent in 1893.\",\"url\":\"https://group.mercedes-benz.com/company/tradition/company-history/1885-1886.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"198\",\"title\":\"Karl Benz and the First Practical Automobile - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"May 6, 2025 · In 1885, a German mechanical engineer named Karl Benz designed and built the world's first practical automobile powered by an internal-combustion engine.\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/karl-benz-and-automobile-4077066\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"199\",\"title\":\"Haber-Bosch Process (Ammonia) » RFNBOs - HY2GEN\",\"description\":\"In 1909, Fritz Haber successfully demonstrated the synthesis of ammonia from nitrogen and hydrogen in a laboratory setting. He used a high-pressure reaction ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.hy2gen.com/haber-bosch-process\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"200\",\"title\":\"Haber-Bosch Process - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"description\":\"From 1909 until 1913, Carl Bosch transformed Fritz Haber's tabletop demonstration of a method to fix nitrogen using high-pressure chemistry into an important ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/chemistry/haber-bosch-process\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"201\",\"title\":\"HABER \u0026 BOSCH - Haber-Bosch process - IDSIA\",\"description\":\"Haber was a professor in Karlsruhe when he demonstrated the feasibility of ammonia synthesis in 1909. Bosch, an engineer at BASF in Ludwigshafen, then overcame ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.idsia.ch/~juergen/haberbosch.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"202\",\"title\":\"First Industrial Revolution vs. Second ... - HISTORY CRUNCH\",\"description\":\"Jan 2, 2016 · The First Industrial Revolution centered on textile manufacturing and the innovation of the steam engine, the Second Industrial Revolution focused instead on ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.historycrunch.com/first-industrial-revolution-vs-second-industrial-revolution.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"203\",\"title\":\"The Second Industrial Revolution: The Technological Revolution\",\"description\":\"May 16, 2022 · All of these new technologies led to a significant increase in mass production and a decrease in costs. This allowed businesses to have an ...\",\"url\":\"https://richmondvale.org/second-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"204\",\"title\":\"Economic Policies During the Second Industrial Revolution - Lesson\",\"description\":\"Feb 4, 2025 · Learn about the economic policies during the Second Industrial Revolution, monetary policy, tariffs, the Gilded Age, and how the Sherman Antitrust Act was used.The Gilded Age · Monetary Policy · Attempts to Rein In Big Business\",\"url\":\"https://study.com/academy/lesson/economic-policy-industrialization-in-the-us-during-the-industrial-revolution.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"205\",\"title\":\"The Second Industrial Revolution, 1870-1914 - US History Scene\",\"description\":\"Major Technological Advances of the Second Industrial Revolution · 1870s. Automatic signals, air brakes, and knuckle couplers on the railroads; the Bessemer and ...\",\"url\":\"https://ushistoryscene.com/article/second-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"206\",\"title\":\"Second Industrial Revolution: what it is and characteristics\",\"description\":\"The Second Industrial Revolution, from 1870 to 1914, was characterized by geographic spread, mass production, transportation, new materials, and ...\",\"url\":\"https://humanidades.com/en/second-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"207\",\"title\":\"Cultural \u0026 Societal Changes of the Second Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"Sep 26, 2019 · From roughly 1870 to 1914 the Second Industrial Revolution produced several more noteworthy inventions, new processes and manufacturing methods ...Missing:  key characteristics\",\"url\":\"https://phlextek.com/blog/f/cultural-societal-changes-of-the-second-industrial-revolution\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"208\",\"title\":\"IB History - First and Second Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"The Second Industrial Revolution was characterised by both internal migration (e.g., southern Blacks move to northern cities) and immigration from Europe. Over ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.internationalschoolhistory.com/ib-history---first-and-second-industrial-revolution.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"209\",\"title\":\"Social Reform in the Second Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"During the Second Industrial Revolution, social reform was needed due to poor treatment of citizens, especially children, who worked long hours in factories ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.okhistory.org/learn/childlabor1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"210\",\"title\":\"Social Effects of Industrialization - AP World Study Guide - Fiveable\",\"description\":\"Industrialization gave rise to new social classes and greater social stratification. Wealth became increasingly tied to industrial ownership rather than land ...\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/ap-world/unit-5/social-effects-industrialization-1750-1900/study-guide/yz9JKbQAG6X4xBMGJGWo\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"211\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Slow Real Wage Growth during the Industrial Revolution\",\"description\":\"During the Industrial Revolution, real wages grew slowly, with real GDP per worker growing faster than real consumption earnings, and real product wages ...\",\"url\":\"https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/soc/economics/research/centres/cage/wp474.2020.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"212\",\"title\":\"Child Labor during the British Industrial Revolution – EH.net\",\"description\":\"Economic historians argue it was the rise in the standard of living that accompanied the Industrial Revolution that allowed parents to keep their children home.\",\"url\":\"https://eh.net/encyclopedia/child-labor-during-the-british-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"213\",\"title\":\"Optimism or pessimism? A composite view on English living ...\",\"description\":\"Mar 3, 2021 · Also, further supporting the pessimists' case, health levels stagnated after the 1820s, annual working time reached new heights in the 1830s, ...\",\"url\":\"https://ehes.org/2021/03/03/optimism-or-pessimism-a-composite-view-on-english-living-standards-during-the-industrial-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"214\",\"title\":\"British wellbeing 1780-1850: Measuring the impact of ... - CEPR\",\"description\":\"May 22, 2016 · The British experience shows that industrialisation per se does not bring immediate gains in living standards if industrialisation is not ...\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/british-wellbeing-1780-1850-measuring-impact-industrialisation-wages-health\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"215\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Argument of Bourgeois Dignity: Why Economics Can't Explain ...\",\"description\":\"We need to explain the astonishing enrichment in bourgeois countries from 1800 to the present, such as Norway's move from $3 a day in 1800 to $137 in 2006.\",\"url\":\"https://www.deirdremccloskey.com/docs/precis.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"216\",\"title\":\"Is There Still Life in the Pessimist Case? Consumption during ... - jstor\",\"description\":\"Recent research on the standard-of-living controversy has argued that a marked improvement in the economic well-being of British workers began shortly after.\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/2122329\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"217\",\"title\":\"How has life expectancy changed over time?\",\"description\":\"Sep 9, 2015 · In the 1840s around 15% of babies died before their first birthday compared with 0.4% in 2011, demonstrating the vast improvements made in ...Missing:  empirical | Show results with:empirical\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/birthsdeathsandmarriages/lifeexpectancies/articles/howhaslifeexpectancychangedovertime/2015-09-09\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"218\",\"title\":\"The British Industrial Revolution in Global Perspective\",\"description\":\"Why did the industrial revolution take place in eighteenth-century Britain and not elsewhere in Europe or Asia? In this convincing new account Robert Allen ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/british-industrial-revolution-in-global-perspective/29A277672CCD093D152846CE7ED82BD9\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"219\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The British Industrial Revolution in Global Perspective\",\"description\":\"The second was geographical–Britain had vast and readily worked coal deposits. In pre-industrial Europe, real wages moved inversely to the population. As ...\",\"url\":\"https://users.nber.org/~confer/2006/SEGs06/allen.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"220\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The British Industrial Revolution in Global Perspective\",\"description\":\"In particular, wages were remarkably high in Britain, while coal and energy were cheap. This price structure created a demand for labour-saving, energy-using ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thebritishacademy.ac.uk/documents/2079/pba167p199_0.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"221\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Why did the Industrial Revolution Start in Britain? - ORBi\",\"description\":\"Dec 7, 2015 · The Industrial Revolution in Britain is attributed to factors like geography, demography, agricultural progress, demand, trade, institutions, ...\",\"url\":\"https://orbi.uliege.be/bitstream/2268/188592/1/Why%2520Did%2520the%2520Industrial%2520Revolution%2520Start%2520in%2520Britain.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"222\",\"title\":\"'Nation of makers': Britain industrialised over a century earlier than ...\",\"description\":\"Apr 5, 2024 · The research shows that 17th century Britain saw a steep decline in agricultural peasantry, and a surge in people who manufactured goods ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cam.ac.uk/stories/nation-of-makers-industrial-britain\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"223\",\"title\":\"Publications: Industrial Revolution - Deirdre McCloskey\",\"description\":\"The slave trade, colonial exploitation, overseas trade, rising thrift, improved racial stock—no such material cause works to explain he modern world. We must ...\",\"url\":\"http://deirdremccloskey.org/articles/revolution.php\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"224\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://deirdremccloskey.com/docs/precis.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"225\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Reconstructing the Industrial Revolution: Analyses, Perceptions and ...\",\"description\":\"The Industrial Revolution continues to be analysed by economic historians deploying the conceptual vocabularies of modern social science, particularly economics ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.lse.ac.uk/Economic-History/Assets/Documents/WorkingPapers/Economic-History/2004/WP8404.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"}],\"images\":[{\"id\":\"f07de69283fc\",\"caption\":\"Spinning jenny\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Spinning_jenny.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"3a8147f3aede\",\"caption\":\"Ironbridge Gorge, site of the world's first major cast-iron bridge completed in 1779, illustrating Britain's iron resources\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Ironbridge_6.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"8df75ec5565c\",\"caption\":\"Newcomen atmospheric engine\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Newcomens_Dampfmaschine_aus_Meyers_1890.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"238ac02595b4\",\"caption\":\"Watt steam engine\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Maquina_vapor_Watt_ETSIIM.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"f07de69283fc\",\"caption\":\"Spinning jenny\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Spinning_jenny.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"8c1ba8f40293\",\"caption\":\"Power loom weaving\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Powerloom_weaving_in_1835.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"3a8147f3aede\",\"caption\":\"Iron Bridge, the world's first major cast-iron structure, completed in 1779\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Ironbridge_6.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"b783f941ad17\",